 # Changelog
 
 Dated, factual, one line per change. Newest first.
+
+## 2026-11-12 - Phase 4, Block D (housekeeping, disclosure rule, W6 mobile-money/TIN evidence, W9 real-data targeting model)
+- Housekeeping: every file at the root of `<workspace>\` and the former `_records\` folder moved to `Behavioral\_archive\process_records\` (SHA-256 checked, `D0_1_hash_check.csv`); the records both projects share are copied to `MultiAgent\_archive\process_records\`; the root now holds only `Behavioral\` and `MultiAgent\`; `_archive\` is git-ignored in both. Block reports and `REANALYSIS_PLAN.md` are read from and written to `Behavioral\_archive\process_records\` from now on.
+- Data terms: `docs/data_terms.md` and `data/raw/SOURCES.csv` record the seven National Data Archive terms verbatim for FinScope, ILFS, Census and the MoF workbook (redistributable: no; publication-copy obligation confirmed); `docs/publishing_checklist.md` (new) lists what must happen before the repository or app is public. The ILFS 2024 citation mismatch stays open.
+- Block C decisions: `macro.context_target_pct = 13.5` with its MoF 2026/27 citation is written to `macro_inputs.json` as context (not used in the gap); the peer-average benchmark stays the headline.
+- Disclosure rule (D1): `config.yaml disclosure:` (`min_base` 10, `low_precision_numerator` 10) read by `src/disclosure.py`; applied to the region x activity and active-benchmark cells (including registration rates), `finscope_summary.json` / `finscope_feature_store.json`, region TIN rates, ILFS and TIN-by-segment tables and all new outputs. Dashboard threshold 8 replaced by the config value; suppressed cells read "suppressed (fewer than 10 respondents)"; low-precision cells carry a visible note (`pages/3_Active.py`). New `tests/test_disclosure.py`.
+- W6 (D2): `src/04_models/tin_mobile_money.py` (survey-weighted Firth logit, reconstructed design SEs, average marginal effect) writes `outputs/stats/tin_mobile_money.json` and `outputs/tables/tin_mobile_money.csv`, labelled observational / first-pass / not causal. `run_causal_inference_analysis` and its `causal_inference` output removed; the Home page's three typed causal figures replaced by the real estimates. New `tests/test_tin_mobile_money.py`.
+- W9 (D3): `src/04_models/targeting_model.py` trains L2 logistic regression and gradient boosting on all 9,915 FinScope adults (leakage audit, stratified 20% test set, repeated stratified 5-fold CV, weighted and unweighted metrics, seeds in `config.yaml targeting:`), publishes aggregates only (`outputs/stats/targeting_model.json`, `outputs/tables/targeting_deciles.csv`, `data/processed/agent_cells.json`). `build_segmentation_model` and `finscope_targeting_population_loader.py` (5,000 synthetic rows) retired (loader moved to `_archive/retired_code/`); the agent-based and tier-migration simulations resample real respondents' attributes. Entry page rebuilt on the new outputs. New `tests/test_targeting.py`.
+- Assumptions: 55 constants (did.*, psm.*, sc.*, seg.*, lifecycle.*, synthetic.urban_share, agents.age_min/max) moved from `assumptions:` to `retired_assumptions:` and listed as RETIRED in `docs/assumptions_register.csv`; the sensitivity analysis dropped the segmentation and causal groups and was re-run; the BLOCKED list was recomputed. Claims map gains `block_d_*` columns. `docs/block_d_code_changes.diff` lists the code changes.
+- Tests: `conftest.py` gains a shared one-run pipeline fixture and a lighter targeting configuration for the throw-away copies; `tests/test_idempotency.py`, `test_from_processed.py`, `test_assumptions.py` updated for the new and retired outputs. `run_all.py` has two new steps (2a, 2b) and no longer runs the old targeting-population step; `src/05_simulation/` is gone.
 
